      <title>Council plans annual black bin collections</title>
      <link>https://www.newsbiscuit.com/post/council-plans-annual-black-bin-collections</link>
      <description>West Moorland District Council urgently needs to save money following ill-advised investments in casinos, wind farms, industrial units, a chip shop, and a rail tunnel under Buckinghamshire. Councillors had debated cutting black bin collections from every two weeks to every three weeks or even every four weeks. But the savings did not stack up. To balance the books, the council has voted to empty black bins once a year, on April 1st. ‘We are doing this to boost recycling,’ said the Member...</description>
